;; recite (PLAN-018 W6) — a tail goal-restatement, the todo.md analogue.
;;
;; Manus: "recite the goal at the TAIL" — keep the mission's objective in the
;; recency zone so a long tape does not let the model drift from what it was
;; asked. This produces a COMPACT restatement to APPEND at the end of the tape
;; (never in the cached prefix — it changes each turn as progress advances, so it
;; must live after the last cache breakpoint, exactly like a rolling todo).
;;
;; ZERO inference: the restatement is a DATA projection of the recorded history —
;; the opening user prompt (the goal) + a cheap progress tally (turns taken, files
;; touched, the last few tool heads). NOT an LLM summary.
;;
;; Returns a string (the tail block), or "" when there is no goal yet.

(let [nodes data/nodes

      ;; the GOAL: the first user prompt that opened the mission.
      goal (->> nodes
                (filter (fn [n] (and (string? (get n "prompt"))
                                     (> (count (get n "prompt")) 0))))
                first
                (#(if % (get % "prompt") "")))

      ;; cheap progress signal: how many program turns, and the distinct shell
      ;; command heads run across the tape (what the agent has been DOING).
      turns (count nodes)

      heads (->> nodes
                 (mapcat (fn [n] (get n "form_shells")))
                 (filter (fn [h] (and (string? h) (> (count h) 0))))
                 distinct)

      recent-heads (take 8 heads)]

  (if (= goal "")
    ""
    (str "## Current objective (recited)\n"
         goal "\n\n"
         "Progress: " turns " turns"
         (if (> (count recent-heads) 0)
           (str " - commands used: " (join ", " recent-heads))
           "")
         "\n\nStay on this objective; do not drift.")))
